WHAT IT SAYS, IN SHORT

Free, with no limit on machines or instances: an individual acting on their own
account, whatever they earn; an organisation that does not operate for profit; a
public institution not concerned with collecting or distributing money; and a
company below USD 5,000,000 in annual revenue.

A commercial licence is required above that threshold, for public institutions
that handle money, for defence and law enforcement, for offering Mehengram or a
service built on it to third parties, and for including it in a product sold for
a fee.

Some uses are excluded at any price, whoever you are — section 6 of the
agreement. Your data and anything you write against the plug-in interface remain
entirely yours — sections 4 and 5.

This summary binds nobody and decides nothing. The agreement does. Read EULA.txt.
